  "enhanced_information": "Chemotherapy primarily targets rapidly dividing cells, which explains why certain organs and cell types exhibit varying susceptibility. Cardiac myocytes are post-mitotic and do not divide, making them highly resistant to chemotherapeutic agents. In contrast, enterocytes and hematopoietic cells have high turnover rates and are therefore more susceptible to chemotherapy. Hair follicle cells also divide rapidly, making them susceptible, while liver hepatocytes, although capable of regeneration, are differentiated and exhibit moderate resistance. Thus, the most resistant cell type to chemotherapeutic agents is cardiac myocytes."
